1
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:25,720
YAMU!

2
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:28,477
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:29,880
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,620
Your moves!

5
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:12,357
What a lovely day this is for a duel,

6
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:15,097
especially on an occasion
such as this when two

7
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:18,004
old friends are battling
it out to the very end.

8
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:22,420
It's challenges like this that puts
to the test the ties that bind us.

9
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:25,057
It doesn't matter to me who wins or loses,

10
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:29,640
because in the end I know it is
I who shall emerge victorious.

11
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:33,420
And you, young Yugi,
who shall be vanquished.

12
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:37,700
The game is really too close.

13
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:40,457
Yeah, they're both playing
at the top of their form.

14
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:42,537
I mean, either one of them could win.

15
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:43,450
You're right.

16
00:01:43,533 --> 00:01:46,117
I don't think I've ever
seen such an exciting duel.

17
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,197
And who would have thought
that at this point,

18
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:50,537
Joey would have more life
points left than Yugi?

19
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:51,796
Truly extraordinary.

20
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:57,940
Go ahead and toss it, you.

21
00:01:58,140 --> 00:01:59,400
It won't surprise me.

22
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,077
I know your cards by heart.

23
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:01,990
True.

24
00:02:02,073 --> 00:02:03,537
You'll also know it's my favorite.

25
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:06,100
And it's one of my most powerful cards.

26
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:08,260
Dark Magician! Attack mode!

27
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:09,730
Figures.

28
00:02:09,813 --> 00:02:12,977
You always count on the Dark
Magician when you're in a tight spot.

29
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:14,120
But not this time.

30
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:16,614
Even he's no match for my Skull Dragon.

31
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:17,917
Are you sure?

32
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,588
In a duel, the monster with the
lowest attack strength loses.

33
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:25,257
That's one of the first lessons you ever
taught me about duel monsters, Yu-Gi.

34
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:27,317
Your past has come back to haunt you.

35
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,820
Let's see who spooks whom, don't forget.

36
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:32,537
I also taught you how
to protect your weaker

37
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:35,208
monsters by enhancing
them with magic cards.

38
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:36,380
Don't tell me.

39
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:37,993
You know what's coming.

40
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:42,660
Magical hats, protect and
conceal the Dark Magician.

41
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,337
I usually like this trick.

42
00:02:47,420 --> 00:02:48,260
Good move.

43
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:50,840
That'll sure slow Joey down big time.

44
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:54,380
My hat's off to you, Yugi boy.

45
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:56,640
It's your pick, Joey.

46
00:02:57,220 --> 00:03:00,926
So tell me, which hat do you
think is hiding the Dark Magician?

47
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:05,537
I was hoping to end this duel
before he drew the magical hats.

48
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:10,077
Now I gotta depend on luck, not dueling
skill, to help me find his Dark Magician.

49
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:11,800
Come on, pick a hat.

50
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:16,598
Okay, guess I just gotta
take him down one at a time.

51
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:18,230
Attack!

52
00:03:18,313 --> 00:03:19,300
Molten fireballs!

53
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:23,920
One down.

54
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:29,689
From the looks of
things, you picked wrong.

55
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:32,980
That leaves three. Nuts.

56
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:35,557
This'll give you another
turn to fight back.

57
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:37,758
That may have been Joey's last shot.

58
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:40,717
Whenever a duelist gives
Yugi time to recover,

59
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,877
he always comes back stronger than ever.

60
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:45,497
But if Joey loses, how
can he save his sister?

61
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:49,140
No matter who wins this game,
somebody loses everything.

62
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:00,157
So now that your attack on
my Dark Magician has failed,

63
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:03,617
is there any other play you want
to make before I end your turn?

64
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:06,757
Now that you mention it, I did
have one more move in mind.

65
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:09,237
I hope I'm doing the right
thing here by playing his card.

66
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:13,980
I mean, it could be a mistake,
but I play Garuzis in attack mode.

67
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:18,010
Your turn.

68
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:20,420
Why play that card?

69
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:21,937
Oh, you're right.

70
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:23,397
What could I have been thinking?

71
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:26,260
The Dark Magician has an
attack power of 2,500.

72
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:31,000
And Garoozies only has an
attack strength of 1,800. Yes?

73
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:34,137
I guess you have no choice
but to attack Garoozies.

74
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:37,617
I'm almost giving you the game, but
I got no one to blame but myself.

75
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:38,740
So go ahead, you.

76
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:39,730
Bring it on.

77
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:41,900
Attack me with your Dark Magician.

78
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:44,537
That's what I get for my bonehead move.

79
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:45,450
Hmm.

80
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:50,701
An attack would bring Joey
down to 50 life points.

81
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:53,517
But it would also draw
out the Dark Magician,

82
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:56,557
which would let Joey counterattack
with his black skull,

83
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:58,777
wiping out all of Yugi's life points.

84
00:04:58,860 --> 00:04:59,697
What's the matter?

85
00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:00,610
Bring it on.

86
00:05:00,693 --> 00:05:02,100
I can't stop your attack.

87
00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:04,457
That bluff might have
worked on somebody else,

88
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:06,897
but not somebody who's
known him as long as I have.

89
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:09,417
Sorry, Joey, but I'm not
going to fall for that one.

90
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:13,912
Instead, I'll put this card inside one
of the magical hats and end my turn.

91
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:16,380
Ah, he was too smart for me.

92
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:18,880
Time to pick another hat, Joey. Great.

93
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:22,717
Now he's got something else hidden
under those hats I gotta worry about.

94
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:25,094
And knowing Yugi, it's probably a trap.

95
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:27,330
But wait.

96
00:05:27,413 --> 00:05:28,380
Yugi knows me.

97
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:31,317
And he would know that I would
know that he's laying a trap.

98
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:33,737
So maybe he didn't play a trap after all.

99
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:35,820
Maybe it's a monster card instead.

100
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:40,697
But what if he knows that I would think
that, so it really is a trap card?

101
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:44,900
Except if he knows that I know,
that he knows what I know...

102
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:46,470
Ah, forget it.

103
00:05:46,553 --> 00:05:47,794
I'm just gonna attack.

104
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:50,320
Black Skull Dragon, attack!

105
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:53,520
Molten Fireballs!

106
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,860
Nothing. I missed again.

107
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,777
That's the way life goes, Joey.

108
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:10,580
Never as you've planned.

109
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:13,940
The world is a very
arbitrary place, isn't it?

110
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:17,477
It's a place where you can be locked
in battle with your dearest friend,

111
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:20,460
for stakes neither can afford to lose. Oh,

112
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:22,517
I know you'd like to think
that your friendship would be

113
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:25,777
enough to sustain you through
any mishap or misfortune,

114
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:28,820
but that's not the way
the world works. No,

115
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:32,577
the world is a place where fate
intervenes when you least expect it,

116
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:36,320
with consequences that can
turn your world upside down.

117
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:39,337
Just when you think you've
etched the perfect portrait

118
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:42,538
of your future and your life
couldn't get any better.

119
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:46,860
Just when you let down your guard
at last and open your heart.

120
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:48,720
When against all odds,

121
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:51,417
you've found that one
special person in all

122
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:54,140
the world that fills your heart with joy.

123
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:58,857
The person you know you are destined
to spend the rest of your life with.

124
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:00,740
That's when tragedy strikes.

125
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:06,060
When fate hits you with a cold slap
of reality and shows you who's boss.

126
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:11,180
Yes, the world has taught me that only
the strong and the ruthless survive.

127
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:17,800
In memory of all I have lost, I fight on
with all I possess, and I intend to win.

128
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:20,620
I'm not gonna miss this time, Yugi.

129
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:22,879
I'm gonna blast your dark magician.

130
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,660
Dragon, attack!

131
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:26,560
The hat on the far left!

132
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:29,440
Go now, Molten Fireball!

133
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:50,020
You activated my trap.

134
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:52,036
Spellbinding circle.

135
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:56,615
That dropped my skull's attack points.

136
00:07:56,820 --> 00:07:58,761
Now he's vulnerable to an attack.

137
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:00,780
I can't risk both my monsters.

138
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,620
Garoozy's defense mode.

139
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:05,839
Now you're on the defensive,
and it's a nice change.

140
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:10,197
Yugi's Spellbinding Circle has
wiped out Joey's attack advantage.

141
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:13,137
No doubt about that, but
it's still a close match.

142
00:08:13,220 --> 00:08:14,050
You said it.

143
00:08:14,133 --> 00:08:16,437
Yugi could attack with the Dark Magician.

144
00:08:16,520 --> 00:08:19,197
But what good would that
attack really do him?

145
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:23,257
Both the Dark Magician and the Skull
Dragon have equal attack strengths.

146
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:24,557
As strong as they are,

147
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:27,697
a battle between the two of them
would just result in a standoff.

148
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:29,020
A stalemate, huh?

149
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:33,617
Somehow, one of them is going to have to
do something to tip things in their favor.

150
00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:34,530
Hmm.

151
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:35,610
Oh.

152
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:38,407
Yugi's the toughest
opponent I've ever faced.

153
00:08:39,140 --> 00:08:40,220
But I'll beat him.

154
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:42,777
Joey's really learned a
lot the past few weeks.

155
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:43,997
He plays like a pro.

156
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:47,877
But in the duel against Pegasus, it's
going to take more than an expert duelist.

157
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:49,517
It's going to take someone who can also

158
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:52,137
stand up to the power
of his Millennium Item.

159
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:56,520
Joey, you've dueled well, but the
tide of this battle is about to turn.

160
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:58,660
Most impressive.

161
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:01,297
Despite the bond that these two share,

162
00:09:01,380 --> 00:09:04,057
My Millennium Eye tells
me that they are indeed

163
00:09:04,140 --> 00:09:06,905
dueling each other with
everything they've got.

164
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:10,520
With my grandpa's soul at
stake, I really have no choice.

165
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:11,980
I have to win this.

166
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,261
All right, Joey.

167
00:09:13,460 --> 00:09:14,460
Prepare yourself.

168
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:17,900
I'm going to obliterate
your dragon. You what?

169
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:20,180
I'm ready for you. Bring it on.

170
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:26,400
This is it, Joey.

171
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:31,020
The card I drew will vanquish your
skull dragon once and for all.

172
00:09:50,380 --> 00:09:56,260
I play the Book of Secret Arts,
and with its ancient magic,

173
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:59,774
my Dark Magician becomes 300
100 attack points stronger.

174
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:07,340
Go, Dark Magician!

175
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:10,220
Attack the Black Skull Dragon!

176
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:19,000
Joey, Black Skull is beaten.

177
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:21,880
Excellent work, Yugi-Boy.

178
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:24,139
You took out his very best monster.

179
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:31,217
Man, I was counting on that Black
Skull Dragon to win this duel.

180
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:35,217
Now, not only is he gone, but I got a
souped-up Dark Magician to worry about.

181
00:10:35,300 --> 00:10:37,680
Joey's kept me down all match long.

182
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,200
But now I finally have the advantage.

183
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:44,640
Not only is my Dark Magician
300 points stronger than normal,

184
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:48,320
but he's ready to show off
a few hidden powers, too.

185
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:50,920
Poor Joey.

186
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:52,717
He really got slammed there.

187
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,717
You think this duel's over for him?

188
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:57,035
Well, it depends on what he does next.

189
00:10:57,180 --> 00:10:58,180
What do you mean?

190
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:02,457
Losing that Black Skull Dragon was a
heavy loss, but not a critical one.

191
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:07,060
If Joey can just pull himself
together, he can still win this duel.

192
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:12,273
Man, how could I go from top of the
heap to down in the dumps in one turn?

193
00:11:12,620 --> 00:11:14,180
I'm never gonna win now.

194
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:15,900
Big Brother.

195
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:17,670
Serenity.

196
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,300
Joey, I miss you so much.

197
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:21,461
Don't forget me.

198
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:23,980
Pinky Swim? Sure.

199
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:26,476
We'll always look out for each other.

200
00:11:28,940 --> 00:11:30,060
What am I thinking?

201
00:11:30,380 --> 00:11:31,321
I can't give up.

202
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:33,108
My sister's counting on me.

203
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:40,708
No matter how bad things look,
I gotta keep fighting for her.

204
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:43,300
Okay, let's do this.

205
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:46,460
Part of the cards, don't fail me now.

206
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,280
Huh? Huh?

207
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:51,780
Oh, yeah.

208
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:53,690
Hmm.

209
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:59,520
All right, Yu-Gi, time
to kiss the baby. Go!

210
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:02,400
Baby dragon, attack mode.

211
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:06,730
Hmm.

212
00:12:07,140 --> 00:12:08,960
And I'm laying this down, too.

213
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:13,810
Hmm.

214
00:12:13,893 --> 00:12:16,797
That second card Joey threw
must be the Time Wizard.

215
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,477
He always plays them together.

216
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:20,377
I have to do something
before he activates its

217
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:23,197
magic and warps that baby
dragon into its adult form.

218
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:28,020
Sorry, Joey, but my Dark Magician
will destroy your baby dragon!

219
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:30,760
Dark Magic Attack!

220
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:36,100
Sorry, Yug, but you just
walked into a trap. What?

221
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:38,673
Go ahead and let him have it, Garoozies.

222
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:40,240
Kunai with Chain!

223
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:46,350
Oh!

224
00:12:49,260 --> 00:12:50,180
Clever move.

225
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:54,558
Joey knew I was expecting the Time
Wizard, so he threw a trap instead.

226
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:58,060
Shame on you, Yugi boy.

227
00:12:58,300 --> 00:13:02,437
Using the knowledge you have of Joey's
deck to predict what card he would play.

228
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:04,160
And to no avail, too.

229
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:07,840
At least when I prophesize
cards, I'm always right.

230
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:15,980
Well, Yug, I'd say that last move brings
us to the homestretch, wouldn't you?

231
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:16,990
I would.

232
00:13:17,073 --> 00:13:17,960
And now, Joey,

233
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:22,887
let's finish this match and find out
which one of us will duel against Pegasus.

234
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:27,620
Hey, Yug. Joey.

235
00:13:27,940 --> 00:13:30,477
Just know it's been a
real honor dueling you.

236
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:31,390
Likewise.

237
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:32,800
How cool.

238
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:37,120
Even now, in the midst of
battle, they're friends first.

239
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:41,980
I know neither of us want to
lose this match, but if I do,

240
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:43,985
I'm glad it was to you, buddy.

241
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:47,655
Now let's do like you said,
Yugi, and finish this duel.

242
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:51,020
And maybe this draw will do just that.

243
00:13:51,460 --> 00:13:53,578
Guess it's just one way to find out.

244
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:54,670
Here goes.

245
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,190
Unreal!

246
00:14:00,273 --> 00:14:02,357
I pulled the one card
in my whole deck that

247
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:05,017
really can finish this
duel and decide a winner.

248
00:14:05,100 --> 00:14:07,400
You mean you pulled? That's right.

249
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:09,000
The Time Wizard.

250
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:11,920
The Time Wizard?

251
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:18,317
Kind of strange that this is all
coming down to a card that you gave me.

252
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:19,230
Here, Joy.

253
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:21,074
Add this to your deck.

254
00:14:21,740 --> 00:14:23,740
It can be helpful in a tight spot.

255
00:14:24,380 --> 00:14:25,760
Wow. Thanks, Yuge.

256
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:28,076
You're always being such a pal to me.

257
00:14:30,680 --> 00:14:31,940
You were right, Yuge.

258
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:35,317
That card you gave me saved my Kista
quite a few times in this tournament.

259
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:40,057
And now with my baby dragon on the field
and both of us just life points away from

260
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:42,037
winning or losing this duel I'm gonna give

261
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:44,649
it one last spin and
hope it saves me again

262
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:48,697
So cross your fingers and
get set to adjust your

263
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:52,880
clocks because here it
comes Go time roulette

264
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:09,840
Come on, Time Warp.

265
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:19,940
All right, jackpot.

266
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:22,617
Go, Time Warp.

267
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:23,940
Time magic.

268
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:31,950
Sorry,

269
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:36,864
Yug, but I'm afraid my Time Warp that has
made the Dark Magician a sickly old man.

270
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:38,680
Look at the Dark Magician!

271
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:40,782
He's aged like a thousand years.

272
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:42,842
He's no match for Joey's dragon.

273
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,420
All right.

274
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:50,400
I can hardly believe it.

275
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:52,280
This is it.

276
00:15:52,620 --> 00:15:54,400
I'm really gonna do it.

277
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:59,340
All I gotta do is attack, and
I'll have actually beat Yugi.

278
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:02,117
I'm gonna win! Attack!

279
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:04,180
Noxious Nostril Gust!

280
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:09,940
I counter with Makiyou, the Magical Mist!

281
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:13,370
Huh?

282
00:16:13,453 --> 00:16:15,340
My attack's getting smothered.

283
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:18,420
What's going on?

284
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:22,700
How did you play Makiyou while
it was still my turn? With magic.

285
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:27,597
A magic so powerful that it took my dark
magician a thousand years to learn it.

286
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:28,510
Say, what?

287
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:31,073
That time warp did age my dark magician.

288
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:34,640
But it made him stronger, not weaker.

289
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:37,420
And with age comes great wisdom.

290
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:43,180
A thousand years of wisdom that have
transformed him into the Dark Sage.

291
00:16:44,860 --> 00:16:48,657
An ultimate magician whose new
powers let me play one magic

292
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:52,152
card during every one of your
turns and every one of mine.

293
00:16:52,260 --> 00:16:55,201
And the magic card I chose
to counter your attack?

294
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,140
Makiyou, the Magical Mist!

295
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:59,717
With its enchanted
rainfall upon the field,

296
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:03,859
your dragon's smoke stream was
neutralized before it reached my mage.

297
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:10,080
Now I invoke his powers for my
turn and draw this magic card.

298
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:17,236
You fought a valiant duel, my friend,

299
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:20,320
and this is the hardest
move I've ever had to make.

300
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:22,160
But this ends now.

301
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:28,640
I play Monster Reborn and call the Black
Skull Dragon back from the graveyard.

302
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:31,900
And it's over.

303
00:17:36,580 --> 00:17:38,980
Yugi, go for it.

304
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:40,000
It's cool.

305
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:43,920
All right, Black Skull Dragon!

306
00:17:45,780 --> 00:17:47,940
Molten Fireball attack!

307
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:07,760
I tell you, that was
really tough to watch.

308
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,350
Yeah.

309
00:18:09,433 --> 00:18:11,722
Well, just imagine how
those two must be feeling.

310
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:13,760
I'm just glad it's over.

311
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,725
And I'm so proud of them both.

312
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:19,945
They duel their hardest, but never
once forgot their friendship.

313
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:21,890
Hmm.

314
00:18:21,973 --> 00:18:26,266
Well, touching as that may be, you really
ought to save your tears, little girl.

315
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:30,915
After all, you'll be needing them
once I face Yugi in the dueling arena.

316
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:37,320
Well, Yugi, we knew one of us had to lose.

317
00:18:37,540 --> 00:18:40,477
But the good news is that
one of us got to win, too.

318
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:41,795
Congratulations, man.

319
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:43,512
Here, this is yours now.

320
00:18:44,100 --> 00:18:45,240
Huh? Go ahead.

321
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:46,402
It's all yours.

322
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,697
You show Croquet his card. Huh?

323
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:51,497
And he'll give you three
million bucks in prize money.

324
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:52,410
No, Joey.

325
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:54,060
You should keep it.

326
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:56,046
Your sister needs that money.

327
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:59,337
Yuge, I didn't enter into this
tournament to get rich, Joey.

328
00:18:59,420 --> 00:19:02,497
I'm just here to save my
grandpa and the Kaiba brothers.

329
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:05,404
Please, use this money
for Serenity's operation.

330
00:19:05,840 --> 00:19:06,670
Really?

331
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:08,110
Yugi.

332
00:19:08,780 --> 00:19:10,200
What do you say, Joey?

333
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:12,697
Hey, it's what you've been wanting, buddy.

334
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:15,251
Look at him, always playing the tough guy.

335
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:23,420
Yugi, when I lost the duel, I
lost all hope of saving my sister.

336
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,620
But now, Yugi, thank you.

337
00:19:27,180 --> 00:19:29,260
Now go and take down Pegasus.
